  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\nGodan verb ({結|むす}びつく → {結|むす}びつきます). Intransitive. The pattern is AがBに{結|むす}びつく (A connects to / leads to B) or AとBが{結|むす}びつく (A and B are connected).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {成果|せいか}に{結|むす}びつく: to lead to results\n- {成功|せいこう}に{結|むす}びつく: to lead to success\n- {利益|りえき}に{結|むす}びつく: to be linked to profit\n- {密接|みっせつ}に{結|むす}びつく: to be closely connected\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\nThe transitive counterpart is {結|むす}びつける (to tie together, to connect). {繋|つな}がる is a more general word for being connected, while {結|むす}びつく emphasizes a meaningful or significant bond.",
